<section class="sec--l" aria-labelledby="check-title">
<div class="container">
<div class="head"><h2 id="check-title">Five dimensions</h2><p class="lead">Each answered from your systems: code, tickets, analytics and invoices. Interviews only explain what the data shows.</p></div>
<ol class="numbered">
<li><h3>Delivery</h3><p>Does an idea reach customers sooner, without more rework?</p><p class="small">We read: path to production, tests, the review queue, incidents and reverts.</p></li>
<li><h3>Product</h3><p>Are we building the right thing, and do pilots become products?</p><p class="small">We read: the roadmap against what shipped, feature usage and the list of pilots.</p></li>
<li><h3>People</h3><p>Is it lifting the whole team, or a few?</p><p class="small">We read: who uses what, how much senior time goes to review, and whether rules are shared or personal.</p></li>
<li><h3>Economics</h3><p>Does the spend match the outcomes?</p><p class="small">We read: seat and token spend, cost per change shipped, and hires avoided.</p></li>
<li><h3>Control</h3><p>Is it safe, and will it hold?</p><p class="small">We read: your harness (the rules, permissions, checks and evaluations around your agents), who owns each workflow, and how a wrong output would surface.</p></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>

